    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Integer batchSize = Math.min(200, accountIds.size());
        List<Id> currentBatch = accountIds.sublist(0, batchSize);

        // One SOQL query per execution
        List<Account> accounts = [SELECT Id, AnnualRevenue FROM Account WHERE Id IN :currentBatch];

        // Set Rating based on AnnualRevenue
        for (Account acc : accounts) {
            if (acc.AnnualRevenue != null && acc.AnnualRevenue >= 1000000) {
                acc.Rating = 'Hot';
            } else if (acc.AnnualRevenue != null && acc.AnnualRevenue >= 100000) {
                acc.Rating = 'Warm';
            } else {
                acc.Rating = 'Cold';
            }
        }

        // One DML statement per execution
        update accounts;

        // Chain: enqueue next job if Ids remain
        if (accountIds.size() > batchSize) {
            List<Id> remaining = accountIds.sublist(batchSize, accountIds.size());
            System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(remaining));
        }
    }

    public static Id start(List<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }
        return System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(accountIds));
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **200 per execution** | `Math.min(200, accountIds.size())` caps the batch; the first `sublist` slice is at most 200. |
| **One SOQL / one DML** | A single `SELECT … WHERE Id IN :currentBatch` and a single `update accounts`. |
| **Rating logic** | Null / blank `AnnualRevenue` falls through to `Cold`; thresholds are `>= 1,000,000` and `>= 100,000`. |
| **Chaining** | If more than 200 Ids were in the list, a new `AccountScoringJob` is enqueued with the remainder. No `Test.isRunning()` guard, so the full 250-link chain fires in tests. |
| **`execute(null)`** | The `QueueableContext` parameter is unused, so a `null` context is harmless. The `null`/empty guard on `accountIds` prevents NPE when a job is constructed with `null`. |
| **Serialization size** | 50 000 × 18-char Ids ≈ 900 KB, within the 1 MB limit for a stored Queueable payload. |
| **Test feasibility** | A test calls `Test.setAsyncApexJobs(250)` before `Test.startTest()`, then `AccountScoringJob.start(ids)`, then `Test.stopTest()`. All 250 chained jobs run synchronously within the test transaction. |

