## Analysis

This is a textbook case for the **Composite Tree API** (`/composite/tree`). It satisfies every requirement in a single HTTP call:

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| All-or-nothing per order | `"allOrNothing": true` on each root Account sub-tree |
| One failure doesn't block others | Each sub-tree is an independent transaction; a rollback of one leaves the other committed |
| One API call, two orders | Single `POST` with an array of two Account sub-trees |
| Identified by referenceIds | `"referenceId"` in each sObject's `attributes` |
| Upsert on external ID | Including `Customer_Number__c` (External ID, Unique) in the Account body triggers an upsert |
| Link opportunity to account via reference | `"AccountId": "@acct_1001"` references the upsert result by its `referenceId` |

The two orders appear in the array in the listed order (SO-1001 first, SO-1002 second).

