```apex
public class AccountCountrySync {

    public static void handle() {
        // 1. Identify accounts whose BillingCountry actually changed
        Map<Id, Account> oldMap = Trigger.oldMap;
        List<Id> changedIds = new List<Id>();
        Map<Id, String> newCountry = new Map<Id, String>();
        Map<Id, String> oldCountry = new Map<Id, String>();

        for (Account acc : Trigger.new) {
            String prev = oldMap.get(acc.Id).BillingCountry;
            String curr = acc.BillingCountry;
            if (curr != prev) {
                changedIds.add(acc.Id);
                newCountry.put(acc.Id, curr);
                oldCountry.put(acc.Id, prev);
            }
        }

        if (changedIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // 2. One query – only contacts belonging to the changed accounts
        Map<Id, List<Contact>> contactsByAccount = new Map<Id, List<Contact>>();
        for (Contact c : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :changedIds
        ]) {
            contactsByAccount.put(
                c.AccountId,
                contactsByAccount.get(c.AccountId) ?? new List<Contact>()
            );
            contactsByAccount.get(c.AccountId).add(c);
        }

        // 3. Pick the contacts that need updating
        List<Contact> toUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Id accId : changedIds) {
            List<Contact> contacts = contactsByAccount.get(accId);
            if (contacts == null) {
                continue;
            }
            String newCty = newCountry.get(accId);
            String oldCty = oldCountry.get(accId);

            for (Contact c : contacts) {
                // Update when MailingCountry is blank OR still equals the old country
                if (String.isBlank(c.MailingCountry) || c.MailingCountry == oldCty) {
                    toUpdate.add(new Contact(Id = c.Id, MailingCountry = newCty));
                }
            }
        }

        // 4. Bulk DML
        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

### Why this is safe at 200-account batches with 2.3 M total contacts

| Concern | Why it's fine |
|---|---|
| SOQL rows returned | Only contacts for ≤ 200 accounts (typically < 10 000 rows) |
| SOQL queries | Exactly **1** |
| DML | Single `update` statement (bulk) |
| Heap | At most a few thousand `Contact` objects in the map |
| Recursion | DML on `Contact` won't re-fire `AccountTrigger` |
| `BillingCountry` → `null` | `String.isBlank` covers `null`; `c.MailingCountry == null` is also true, so contacts following the old country get blanked correctly |

