public class EmployerService {

    /**
     * Sets the current primary employer (Organization) for each contact in the map.
     * Leverages NPSP's standard mechanism: updating Contact.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c
     * causes NPSP triggers to create/update affiliations, demote the previous primary
     * to Former with today's end date, and preserve the household relationship.
     *
     * @param employerByContactId Keys are Contact Ids, values are Organization Account Ids.
     */
    public static void setCurrentEmployers(Map<Id, Id> employerByContactId) {
        if (employerByContactId == null || employerByContactId.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Single SOQL: fetch current primary affiliation for all target contacts
        Set<Id> contactIds = employerByContactId.keySet();
        Map<Id, Contact> contactMap = new Map<Id, Contact>(
            [SELECT Id, npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c
             FROM Contact
             WHERE Id IN :contactIds]
        );

        // Build the list of contacts whose primary affiliation needs to change
        List<Contact> contactsToUpdate = new List<Contact>();

        for (Id contactId : employerByContactId.keySet()) {
            Contact c = contactMap.get(contactId);
            if (c == null) {
                continue;
            }

            Id newEmployerId = employerByContactId.get(contactId);
            if (newEmployerId == null) {
                continue;
            }

            // No-op if the organization is already the primary affiliation
            if (c.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c == newEmployerId) {
                continue;
            }

            c.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c = newEmployerId;
            contactsToUpdate.add(c);
        }

        // Single DML: NPSP triggers handle affiliation creation, status changes,
        // end dates, and household preservation.
        if (!contactsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update contactsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

**Why this works within the constraints:**

| Constraint | How it's met |
|---|---|
| ≤ 2 SOQL queries | Exactly **1** (the `SELECT` on Contact) |
| ≤ 2 DML statements | Exactly **1** (the `UPDATE` on Contact) |
| 200 contacts in one call | 200 records is well within the 50,000-row DML limit; the `IN :contactIds` clause handles all IDs in one query |
| Current, primary affiliation created | NPSP's trigger on `npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c` auto-creates the `npe5__Affiliation__c` with `Status = Current` and `Primary = true` |
| Previous primary → Former, end date today | NPSP's trigger demotes the old affiliation automatically |
| Contact stays in household | The household link (`npsp__Parent_Household_Account__c`) is independent of the primary affiliation; NPSP preserves it |
| No duplicate if already primary | The `if (c.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c == newEmployerId)` guard skips the update entirely |
| Null/empty map is a no-op | Early return at the top |

