```apex
public with sharing class RecordAccessService {

    private static final Integer CHUNK_SIZE = 1000;

    /**
     * Returns the subset of recordIds that the running user has edit access to,
     * as determined by the UserRecordAccess object.
     *
     * @param recordIds  Up to 2,000 record IDs (may span multiple objects).
     * @return A set of IDs the user can edit. Never null; empty if input is null/empty
     *         or no records are editable.
     */
    public static Set<Id> editableIds(Set<Id> recordIds) {
        Set<Id> editable = new Set<Id>();
        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {
            return editable;
        }

        List<Id> idList = new List<Id>(recordIds);

        // Chunk to stay within SOQL IN-clause limits (1000 values).
        // For 2,000 IDs this produces at most 2 queries, well within the 20-query budget.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < idList.size(); i += CHUNK_SIZE) {
            Integer end = Math.min(i + CHUNK_SIZE, idList.size());
            List<Id> chunk = idList.sublist(i, end);

            List<UserRecordAccess> accessRows = [
                SELECT RecordId
                FROM UserRecordAccess
                WHERE RecordId IN :chunk
                  AND HasEditAccess = true
            ];

            for (UserRecordAccess access : accessRows) {
                editable.add(access.RecordId);
            }
        }

        return editable;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's addressed |
|---|---|
| **Sharing / permissions** | `with sharing` on the class; `UserRecordAccess` already reflects the full access model (object permissions, ownership, sharing rules, role hierarchy, View All / Modify All, etc.) for the running user. |
| **Null / empty input** | Early return of an empty `Set<Id>` — never null. |
| **SOQL limit** | IDs are chunked in groups of 1 000 for the `IN` clause. 2 000 IDs → at most **2 queries**, well under the 20-query budget. |
| **Multi-object IDs** | `UserRecordAccess.RecordId` is a polymorphic lookup; the single query handles any mix of object types. |
| **Records with no access** | If the user has no access to a record, `UserRecordAccess` has no row for it, so it simply won't appear in results — correctly excluded. |
| **Bulk safety** | No per-record DML or SOQL; a single (or two) query(ies) process all IDs in one pass. |

